Subject: [PATCH] moz.configure: recognize aarch64-apple-ios as a target

mozjs 115's build system has no iOS target: split_triplet only maps
`darwin`->(kernel=Darwin, os=OSX), and the OS EnumString has no `iOS`
member, so `--target=aarch64-apple-ios` dies with "Unknown OS: ios" /
"'iOS' is not a valid value for EnumStringSubclass".

Add an `ios` OS branch (kernel Darwin, os iOS) and the `iOS` enum member.
Because os == "iOS" (not "OSX"), the macOS-SDK requirement and the
`-mmacosx-version-min` injection (both gated on os==OSX in
toolchain.configure) are naturally skipped, so the cross C/C++ compiler's
`-target arm64-apple-ios` drives the platform with the iPhoneOS SDK.

Linker note (NOT part of this patch — handled in the build env): moz's ld64
probe hardcodes `-fuse-ld=ld`, so point clang at the cctools ld64
(`ln -s aarch64-apple-darwin-ld .../bin/ld` + `-B<cctools bin>`) and pass
`--enable-linker=ld64`. cctools ld64 emits the "Logging ld64 options"
signature moz identifies it by.

--- a/build/moz.configure/init.configure
+++ b/build/moz.configure/init.configure
@@ -522,6 +522,9 @@
             # in the first place, even when we didn't.
             sub_configure_alias = sub_configure_alias[: -len(os)] + "mingw32"
             raw_os = "mingw32"
+    elif os.startswith("ios"):
+        canonical_kernel = "Darwin"
+        canonical_os = "iOS"
     elif os.startswith("darwin"):
         canonical_kernel = "Darwin"
         canonical_os = "OSX"
--- a/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/constants.py
+++ b/python/mozbuild/mozbuild/configure/constants.py
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@
     "NetBSD",
     "OpenBSD",
     "OSX",
+    "iOS",
     "SunOS",
     "WINNT",
     "WASI",
